  "verdict": "NO-GO net, but a DIFFERENT result. The overnight premium is the program's FIRST robust gross OOS edge (gross Sharpe IS 0.85 -> OOS 1.78, low kurtosis): the structural-premium prior is VALIDATED. But net of financing it is ~zero on a leveraged account (cost ratio ~1.0 at 2bps swap; P(pass) peaks ~30% = the zero-edge baseline), it is directional equity beta (per-year net sign-flips with the regime), and it carries an overnight-gap left tail (tail-DD 17%). CRUCIAL refinement of the venue pivot: the financing that eats the premium is NOT a retail-CFD tax \u2014 it is the cost of carry of leveraged overnight equity, embedded in the futures basis too (F=S*e^{(r-q)T}). So futures do NOT cleanly rescue it, unlike the HF-reversal case. The only venue that escapes it is holding the cash index unleveraged \u2014 which no propfirm challenge does."
